{"name":"Par Four","hex":"#507069","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"par","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Panamint."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Abbreviation of paragraph.","Abbreviation of parenthesis."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/par"},{"term":"four","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["NATO & ICAO radiotelephony clear code (spelling-alphabet name) for the digit 4."]},{"part":"Numeral","definitions":["A numerical value equal to 4; the number following three and preceding five.","Describing a set or group with four elements."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/four"}],"entries":[{"title":"Par (score)","blocks":[{"text":"In golf, par is the predetermined number of strokes that a proficient golfer should require to complete a hole, a round, or a tournament. For scoring purposes, a golfer's number of strokes is compared with the par score to determine how much the golfer was either \"over par\", \"under par\", or \"even/level par\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Wisconsin_golf_hole_sign.jpg/330px-Wisconsin_golf_hole_sign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Par_(score)"},{"title":"4","blocks":[{"text":"4 (four) is a number, numeral and digit. It is the natural number following 3 and preceding 5. It is a square number, the smallest semiprime and composite number, and is considered unlucky in many East Asian cultures."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a4/Vier.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Scc_score_card_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Scc_score_card_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://th